(* Demand per call site (docs/NOTES.md): `b`'s call of the moded `len` has the prefix `e L, not a L 1`, and
   `a` calls `len`; with one shared demand relation `len^d` would depend negatively on `a`, which depends on
   `len` and so on `len^d` (E0601), although the program is stratified. Likewise `c`'s call demands a
   list computed by an aggregate over `a`. Both calls get their own copy of `len` (`len[int]#1`,
   `len[int]#2`); `a`'s call keeps the shared one *)
e : list int -> rel.
e nil. e (cons 1 nil). e (cons 2 (cons 1 nil)).
a : list int -> int -> rel.
a L N :- e L, len L N.
b : list int -> int -> rel.
b L N :- e L, not a L 1, len L N.
c : int -> int -> rel.
c M K :- M = count { L | a L _ }, len (cons M (cons M nil)) K.
?- b L N.
?- c M K.
